# claude-seat-1: task 1790622956 ("local-up pins the deployer identity, so E-74 cannot recur on a machine whose default identity is another project's")

Closes: 1790622956 (done)

## What landed (branch claude/seat-1, on top of main 5e0b935)

- 49a982d fix: local-up pins the deployer identity (DEFECTS E-74 root cause)
  - scripts/dev.sh: `up_identities` is step [1/7]: it creates `cd-local-deployer` and the four players when missing (`icp identity new --storage plaintext`, before the network starts, because the managed network funds the identities that exist at start), reads the machine default for the report and never changes it. `up_deploy` passes `--identity "$CONTROLLER"` to `icp deploy`, pre-checks an existing stack's controller before touching it, and asserts every backend canister's controller after the deploy. `resolve_controller_identity` signs its `canister status` read per candidate (the read is controller-only, so unsigned it ran as the default identity, the very drift being detected; stdin closed so a password-protected identity fails instead of prompting). `die_foreign_controller` prints the hand-over (`icp canister settings update <c> --add-controller <principal> --identity <holder>` per canister plus `lobby set_admin`) and the `--reset` alternative, worded differently for a network this run rebuilt (the pin did not take) and for leftover state. `up_wire` dies, not warns, on a controller that is not `$CONTROLLER`; reads `get_admin` before the lobby calls and dies on a foreign admin; `set_admin` and `init_microstakes_tables` go through `call_or_die` (both are Ok and idempotent for the admin). `--reset` on a RUNNING network stops it first (`icp network stop` on this project's descriptor; nothing killed by name or port; dies pointing at `factory.sh replica-recycle` if the gateway still answers after 30 s), then deletes the state and marks the network fresh. `up_fund` reads balances with `--of-principal` (the old `--owner` is not an icp 1.3.0 flag, so every balance read 0 and every local-up transferred another 1000 ICP per player), dies when the funder cannot cover the players, and the transfers go through `call_or_die`. `cmd_selftest` gains "the deployer identity is pinned, never inherited": every `icp_local deploy` line carries `--identity "$CONTROLLER"`, and nothing under scripts/ runs `icp identity use <name>` or `icp identity default <name>`. `cmd_doctor` gains an identities step. `icp network start` takes no `--identity` in icp 1.3.0, so the pin lives on the deploy and the controller calls, said in a comment.
  - tools/shots/lib/ids.mjs: `resolveControllerIdentity` signs its status read per candidate (after the backend pin, an unsigned read on this machine would throw IC0542 before consulting any candidate, and local-up would die at the frontend step). Same return shape.
  - tools/shots/lib/frontend-build.mjs: `deployFrontend` creates a not-yet-existing asset canister as `CONTROLLER_IDENTITY` instead of the default identity; an existing one is still resolved.
  - tools/shots/README.md: the controller section says what local-up now does and that the resolver is the harness's own belt.
  - docs/DEFECTS.md: E-74's table row and long-form entry carry the root cause, the fix and the verification. STATUS stays OPEN until a full sweep on a hostile-default machine records it (1790622955).

Canisters untouched: nothing under src/*_canister, Cargo.*, icp.yaml, .icp/ changed. No fund-moving code touched.

## Verified (on this seat's own replica, port 8077, with the machine's default identity `cyclepay-hotwallet`, i.e. another project's; no `icp identity use` was run)

- `./scripts/dev.sh local-up --reset --no-frontend`: exit 0 in 30 s. It stopped the foreign-controlled network left by task 1790621370, deleted the state, restarted, deployed as cd-local-deployer, printed "every backend canister is controlled by cd-local-deployer", wired the archive, "lobby lists 3 table record(s)", refreshed the records, funded (all five identities read 1000000 ICP: the managed network funds every local identity at start).
- `icp canister call lobby get_admin '()' --query -e local --identity cd-local-deployer` -> `opt principal "sg3sw-...-6qe"` = cd-local-deployer's principal; `icp canister status lobby --identity cd-local-deployer` -> Controllers: sg3sw-...-6qe. `icp identity default` still prints cyclepay-hotwallet afterwards.
- `./scripts/dev.sh local-up --no-frontend` a second time (no reset): exit 0, idempotent (existing-network pre-check passed, set_admin Ok, 3 tables).
- `./scripts/dev.sh local-up` (full, with the frontend): exit 0; the asset canister (5uljf-s3777-77775-aaaea-cai) is controlled by cd-local-deployer, so the pinned create in frontend-build.mjs ran live.
- `./scripts/dev.sh selftest`: exit 0 (new step green; the regex was tuned twice so a read-only `icp identity default 2>/dev/null` is not a switch and `default cd-alice` / `use cd-alice` are).
- `make hygiene`: exit 0. `make shots-selftest`: all 13 green. `./scripts/dev.sh doctor`: the identities step prints the pinned deployer and the machine default.
- `bash -n scripts/dev.sh`, `node --check` on both .mjs files.

## NOT verified

- The identity-CREATION branch of `up_identities` (all five identities already exist on this machine; creating a throwaway identity on the machine-global store just to test it was not done). The `pre` branch of `assert_pinned_controller` for a canister no local identity can read, and `die_foreign_controller` against a live foreign stack (the only such stack was the one `--reset` replaced; the message rendering was exercised by evaluating the function with stub values). `make test` was not rerun: nothing under the canisters, tests/ or the frontend changed.
- The task text's verify says to switch the default identity with `icp identity use <other>` in a subshell: NOT done on purpose (the default is shared mutable state across every session on this machine); the hostile condition was already live and is what the runs above ran under.

